Item 3: the Blocker UX2-1 in detail.
- The step 11 page holds 7 words in r6, r7, and r8 on both lessons. It held 147 words (Quest 5) and 140 words (Adventure) in r5, with the header and the box on one page.
- The page content area is 245 mm. The box is about 232 mm tall, and the header block is about 17 mm. The pair needs about 249 mm.
- The rule .guided-writing-step forces a page break before the step (primary_template.html line 580). The 8 mm writing lines of PM decision 2 made the box taller.
- Spec S3 (spec.md line 72) says the title and the box stay on one page. No check covers step 11, and checks-r8.txt passes 17 of 17.
- Fix guidance: shrink the pair by at least 5 mm, and keep the 8 mm pitch. Remove the 4 mm top margin on that header, trim the planner spacing, or let the box split after its header. Add check P18.
- Cutting the draft lines from 6 to 5 saves 8 mm. This changes decision 2, so the PM must choose.

